### Express Components over the Store API (headless)
###
### PhpStorm HTTP client. Fill tests/Http/http-client.env.json (host, accessKey, salesChannelId,
### productId, frontendUrl) and run the requests from top to bottom. The context token is taken
### over from the first request automatically.
###
### The payment itself happens in the Mollie component of the frontend and cannot be sent from
### here. Mount the component with the sessionId and clientAccessToken of step 3, pay, and
### Mollie redirects the browser to the finish route (step 4), which ends on the finishUrl.

### 1. Cart of a new context, the response header carries the context token
GET {{host}}/store-api/checkout/cart
sw-access-key: {{accessKey}}
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.global.set("contextToken", response.headers.valueOf("sw-context-token"));
%}

### 2. Add a product to the cart
POST {{host}}/store-api/checkout/cart/line-item
sw-access-key: {{accessKey}}
sw-context-token: {{contextToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "product",
      "referencedId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

> {%
    client.global.set("contextToken", response.headers.valueOf("sw-context-token"));
%}

### 3. Create the session, finishUrl and errorUrl are the pages of the frontend
POST {{host}}/store-api/mollie/express-components/create-session
sw-access-key: {{accessKey}}
sw-context-token: {{contextToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "finishUrl": "{{frontendUrl}}/checkout/success?orderId={orderId}",
  "errorUrl": "{{frontendUrl}}/checkout/error?orderId={orderId}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("sessionId", response.body.sessionId);
    client.global.set("clientAccessToken", response.body.clientAccessToken);
%}

### 3b. Create the session for an existing order (failed payment), the customer has to be logged in
POST {{host}}/store-api/mollie/express-components/create-session
sw-access-key: {{accessKey}}
sw-context-token: {{contextToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "finishUrl": "{{frontendUrl}}/checkout/success?orderId={orderId}",
  "errorUrl": "{{frontendUrl}}/checkout/error?orderId={orderId}"
}

### 4. The return of Mollie after the payment, a browser opens this, no access key needed.
### Only works for a session that is completed. Do not run it twice, the cart is gone afterwards.
GET {{host}}/api/mollie/express-components/finish/{{salesChannelId}}?cartToken={{contextToken}}&finishUrl={{frontendUrl}}/checkout/success?orderId%3D%7BorderId%7D&errorUrl={{frontendUrl}}/checkout/error?orderId%3D%7BorderId%7D

### 5. Mollie configuration of the sales channel
GET {{host}}/store-api/mollie/config
sw-access-key: {{accessKey}}
sw-context-token: {{contextToken}}
Accept: application/json
